    "description": "Compacts this conversation once your turn ends, then gives you your handoff back and tells you to continue. Use it when a [catnap] note asks you to, or when the person asks for a compaction; before that, carry on: the window has room, and the note tells you when. Call it with your handoff as note (the task, what is done, the next step, open decisions, the files that matter, and every instruction from the person that still applies, in their words); no separate file is needed. Make that call in the same response as your last action (for example the command that runs the tests), as its last tool call, not in a reply of its own: a reply of its own reads the whole conversation once more. You will not see that action's result before the compaction, so your handoff's next step starts with checking it. After calling it, end your reply at once: no more tool calls and no more text. Main conversation only."
   }
